==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-tempt.ogg|Audio (US)}}

* {{rhymes|ɛmpt}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|tempter}} (French: ''[[tenter]]'') < {{etyl|la}} {{term|temptare}}, more correctly {{term|tentare||to handle, touch, try, test, tempt}}, frequentative of {{term|tenere||to hold}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To [[provoke]] someone to do [[wrong]], especially by [[promising]] a [[reward]]; to [[entice]].
#: ''She '''tempted''' me to eat the apple.''
# {{transitive}} To [[attract]]; to [[allure]].
#: ''Its glossy skin '''tempted''' me.''
# {{transitive}} To [[provoke]] something; to [[court]].
#: ''It would be '''tempting''' fate.''

